@title Fraud-Screening Vendor Comparison
@subtitle Fennimore Payments, decision due 2026-11-20
@author Gideon Ashworth, Risk Lead
@date 2026-11-20

For the payments steering group. Fennimore processes about 6 million customer payment transactions a month.

## Side by side

table vendors = Vendor,Fraud caught (%),Good transactions wrongly blocked (%),Fee per 1000 transactions ($),Integration (weeks); Tollgate,91.2,1.9,4.10,6; Vantage Shield,94.8,3.1,6.80,10; Kestrel Risk,89.5,1.2,2.90,4

## Annual fees

At 6 million transactions a month:

data fees = vendor,annual fee; Tollgate,295200; Vantage Shield,489600; Kestrel Risk,208800

chart bar fees unit=$ labels title="Annual fees"

## What the trade-off means

Each wrongly blocked transaction is a customer declined at checkout.

Vantage Shield catches 3.6 points more fraud than Tollgate. That comes with 1.2 points more wrongly blocked transactions and $194400 more in fees a year.

## Recommendation

We lean toward **Tollgate** as the balanced choice. **Kestrel Risk** is the budget fallback if the steering group wants to cut fees by about $86400 a year.

!! If the contract is signed by 2026-12-15, Tollgate and Kestrel Risk would be live before the change freeze on 2027-02-01. Vantage Shield, at 10 weeks, would not.
